From 2a5186e64f36085bd1e88bacce64608d30abe9cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:19:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add admin API for deleting archived messages older than a
 date

Add a `mam` category to the admin GraphQL API (and mongooseimctl) with
four commands that delete messages archived before a given date:
deleteRoomMessages (one room), deleteOldRoomMessages (all rooms of a MUC
service), deleteUserMessages (one user's one-to-one archive) and
deleteOldMessages (all one-to-one archives of a domain). Each returns
the number of deleted messages.

Unlike message retraction, which keeps a tombstone row, these remove
the rows, so they can be used to enforce a retention period.

The deletion is done by the archive backend through the new
mam_delete_messages and mam_muc_delete_messages hooks. The RDBMS
backends delete by the primary key (archive id, message id < cut-off),
and honour delete_domain_limit to delete in batches. Other backends
return a not_supported error.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ETaRHXo1LmPHqZB9SXMucM
